      "explanation": "Carbamazepine is a strong CYP3A4 and P-gp inducer, which decreases apixaban exposure and increases the risk of stroke and other thromboembolic events.",
      "recommendation": "Avoid concomitant use of ELIQUIS with combined P-gp and strong CYP3A4 inducers (e.g., rifampin, carbamazepine, phenytoin, St. John’s wort) because such drugs will decrease exposure to apixaban.",
